 full 360 degree  angle I never got on any wires I was on  this real really cool Advanced machine  that allowed me to lay flat I think fans  will really appreciate the detail and  Nuance of how Black Adam is able to fly  with real rage and power and force  I just dropped him  number four sticking with black Adam's  appearance in the rock of Eternity there  was a scene that was majorly daunting  for the VFX supervisors the moment when  Black Adam grabs one of the mercenaries  by the neck and electrocutes him until  he dissolves and turns into Ash was one  of the most challenging shots they had  to get they had to blend the CGI effects  with an actual person not an alien or  Monster so the challenge was making it  look realistic like an actual human  being was being fried  number five some major brainstorming had  to be done to figure out what they would  look like on screen it was a man who is  bestowed with this power of the helmet  of Naboo which is kind of a blessing and  a curse due to his powers being so  complex and important for the movie's  narrative they went back and forth with  some Stills and comic book shots between  the filmmakers and the visual effects  supervisors in order to figure out what  they were going to do what ended up  happening was some experimentation on a  completely different character a  sequence that unfortunately did not make  the cut before actually applying that CG  to Dr Fate  time for you and I  you and I you know  number six another CGI aspect that could  be overlooked when Black Adam first  appears in the rock of Eternity and the  mercenaries are shooting at him he's  wearing this big black cloak that's  being shredded to Pieces when they shot  it on set it was just Dwayne Johnson in  a cloak but nothing else was actually  happening so they had to go in and add a  bunch of Sparks coming off of him as  well as make the cloth react and Shred  to what was supposed to be going on they  even had to make sure you could see the  fibers