ith unreal the artists were able to  adjust the lighting in real time and  play around with different colors and  effects which gave the production team a  major speed boost when it came to  getting everything done  look at that shoot it's cool thanks  thanks me too number 11 the movie  utilized All The Cutting Edge technology  money could buy Dwayne spilled some  behind the scenes secrets on Instagram  about the high-end technology that was  being used to capture his movements they  used a high-speed phantom camera that  was able to shoot him at 960 frames per  second which is insane compared to the  usual 24 frames per second used for most  movies operating at 40 times the usual  capture rate this was definitely not  your average movie setup  look alive to me because I saved them  number 12 people all over the world  worked on this movie a lot of the work  to create the visual effects were done  remotely there was a visual effects team  in Los Angeles Montreal Vancouver and  Hyderabad India  there were even individual artists  working in Germany Ontario Portland and  Florida because the film was shot during  the coveted pandemic everyone had the  option to work from home even those who  couldn't all of the time were able to do  a hybrid style of work they're only  Heroes and they're villains  you think yourself a hero  Black Adam uses New Age Technology a  Workforce from all over the world a  plethora of green screens and a talented  crew who really know their way around  digital effects throw in the incredible  Black Adam lore taken directly from the  comics what more could you want leave a  comment and let us know what your  favorite CGI moment was
 

